            <ArticleTitle>Same-day combined coronary angioplasty and minimally invasive coronary surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1246-7, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Integrated myocardial revascularization combines the advantages of angioplasty, stenting, and minimally invasive surgery to revascularize patients with multivessel coronary artery disease without cardiopulmonary bypass. This pilot study showed that a new same-day management strategy, consisting of percutaneous coronary intervention followed immediately by minimally invasive surgery, was feasible and provided complete all-arterial revascularization with minimal surgical trauma, short hospital stay, and excellent early therapeutic result in 14 patients with multivessel coronary disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
